      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of what to improve. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Unused `data_plus()` and `data_minus()` methods\n- `assertEquals(false, ...)` / `assertEquals(true, ...)` instead of the more idiomatic `assertFalse` / `assertTrue`\n- No grouping of the 32+ assertions — it's a flat, opaque wall of assertions\n- Many unused imports\n\nI'll write an improved version with grouped, commented assertions and cleaner imports.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file groups assertions into logical categories (time-of-day, day/week, month/year, and other fields) with explanatory comments, replaces `assertEquals(false/true, ...)` with the idiomatic `assertFalse`/`assertTrue`, removes the unused `data_plus()` and `data_minus()` methods, and trims all unused imports — while preserving exactly the same method calls, arguments, and expected outcomes."
    }
